Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:11:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1453/1463] HERESY 1531: the DAW becomes a mixing console.
 Under the lanes every lane is a strip: EQ and compressor inserts, sends to
 the room and the delay after the pan, width, pan, polarity, mute and solo,
 and the fader with its meter on one scale. The room and the delay are returns
 with their own level and mute; the master shows loudness by BS.1770 as it
 plays, a 4x true peak and the correlation of the sides. A strip's devices:
 input (trim, polarity, version chips), an EQ of up to eight RBJ bands drawn
 over the strip's own spectrum, a compressor with its curve, its reduction and
 five starting points, and the output. Undo and redo, A and B, and the stems
 printed with the mix.

What is heard is what is mixed. The page's graph runs the render's order (lab/daw_mix.py, ruach.mix/1): biquads take the render's RBJ coefficients, the stereo panner's law is written out in the render, the room convolves with the very impulse the render uses (/lab/daw/ir), and the delay is Plenio's loop. The compressor and the meters share one kernel (heresy-mixdsp.js), run in an AudioWorklet in a secure context and in a ScriptProcessor when the studio is opened by its network address.

Also: eleven catalogs; suite 1531 (both engines on a tone); 1471 follows the new value; 1499 measures full screen with and without the console.

